16. PERFORMANCE AND PARALLEL LOADING

Performance is a core product requirement.

The homepage must not wait for every section before displaying content.

Use independent concurrent loading.

Suggested loading groups:

- Categories.
- Sponsored campaigns.
- Products.
- Rental properties.
- Swaps.
- Services.
- Wanted requests.
- Jobs.

Each section should render when its own data becomes available.

Keep the intended homepage section order even when requests complete in a different order.

Use:

- Kotlin coroutines.
- Structured concurrency.
- StateFlow.
- Jetpack Compose.
- ViewModels.
- Room where appropriate.
- DataStore for preferences.
- Firestore pagination.
- Bounded queries.
- Stable LazyColumn and LazyRow keys.
- Image caching.
- Background refresh.
- Request cancellation.
- Query deduplication.

Display valid cached content immediately.

Refresh stale content without replacing the entire screen with a loading spinner.

Use skeletons matching the actual card layouts.

Avoid unnecessary Firestore reads and expensive recomposition.

Test on low-end and mid-range Android devices.

